# Hand-maintained (not roxygen-generated).
#
# analyze() is the primary public entry point: one call runs the full
# preprocessing + (optional) normalisation + the caller's analysis. The reader
# and preprocess machinery (readMethArray*, processMethArray*, runPreprocess)
# stays internal -- analyze() composes it, and analyze(..., FUN = NULL) covers
# the "just build the QC'd GDS" case.
export(analyze)

# Read-side adapters: project the QC'd GDS into the container a non-GDS-aware
# downstream package wants -- a dense matrix for FactoMineR/prcomp/irlba, or a
# SummarizedExperiment for limma/sva. Usable on the handle analyze()'s FUN
# receives or on a GDS path.
export(gdsBetaMatrix, gdsSummarizedExperiment)

# Streaming between-array normalisation: reproduces wateRmelon::dasen bit-for-bit
# while reading the GDS one column block at a time (no full matrix, no scratch
# GDS). The default between-array normalizer the analyze() orchestration uses.
export(gdsDasen)

